      <div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q">How do you prove yourself with no work experience?</div><div class="faq-a">Produce the work itself. Pick the role you want, do a real scoped task from it, and get the result evaluated against a professional standard. A scored brief, spec, or analysis proves capability in a way no résumé line can, because the employer judges the work instead of trusting a claim.</div></div>
      <div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q">What is a work sample, and why does it beat a résumé?</div><div class="faq-a">A work sample is a piece of real output from the role you want. It beats a résumé because a résumé is a list of claims taken on faith, while a work sample is evidence a recruiter can open and judge in minutes. They move faster and more confidently on evidence than on claims.</div></div>
      <div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q">How long does it take to build proof of work?</div><div class="faq-a">Weeks, not years. You are not earning another credential, you are producing evidence. A focused person can complete and get feedback on several real tasks in a few weeks, enough to change how a recruiter reads an application.</div></div>
